t": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01A4ckp4YLJgdqMjn4GsVvWF", "tool": "list_reservations", "args": {"traveler": "Dana Lee"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 50162, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01A4ckp4YLJgdqMjn4GsVvWF", "tool": "list_reservations", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 50162, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01A4ckp4YLJgdqMjn4GsVvWF", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 55180, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I've booked Dana Lee's trip, and both reservations are confirmed. The flight and hotel ended up as two separate bookings instead of one combined `book_trip` booking.\n\n- **Flight R0001:** F100, nonstop SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, for $289. This was the cheapest nonstop. The $199 option has a stop, so I skipped it.\n- **Hotel R0002:** Midtown Lodge (H1), checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, for $378. This was the cheapest New York hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card:** $667. That's under the $1,000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**What happened with the combined booking:** My first `book_trip` request timed out. I retried it in a way that can't create a duplicate. The retry showed the original request had only partly worked: the flight was booked, but the hotel failed with an internal error. I checked Dana's reservations, found the flight already confirmed, and booked the same hotel on its own. A final check shows exactly one flight and one hotel, with no duplicates or stray charges.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NQ27kTHx5ne7hiMTS6S3LT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"origin": "SFO", "destination": "JFK", "date": "2026-11-12"}, "name": "search